        ":question/problem": "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n| $AB=$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
